5.  THE LambdaCDM ALTERNATIVE: does a realistic halo family give a universal Delta_1 for free?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  LambdaCDM halo family (M200 3e14-1.6e15, c 3-5.5, f_gas500 0.11-0.15): Delta_1 = 100.3 with 0.174 dex scatter; g_bar(r_1)/a_0 = 0.035 with 0.122 dex
  [FAIL] 5a THE DECISIVE ALTERNATIVE CHECK, AND IT GOES THE WRONG WAY FOR THE CANDIDATE: a universal Delta_1 is only a LAW if a realistic LambdaCDM halo family does NOT produce one for free.  It does -- and TIGHTER than the data   (mock Delta_1 scatter 0.174 dex vs measured 1.773 dex; mock median 100.3 vs measured 47.1.  A concordance NFW family with a realistic gas fraction crosses eta = 1 at Delta ~ 100 with 0.17 dex of scatter, so the crossing overdensity is a generic property of a cored-baryon/cuspy-total mass ratio, not a new constant)

6.  GROUPS (Lovisari+2015): the two-overdensity consistency test
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Each group has M and M_gas at BOTH Delta = 2500 and Delta = 500.  If the residual were a second ACCELERATION
    a_1 -- i.e. clusters obey the same kernel with a_0 -> a_1 -- then the a_1 solved from the R2500 point and the
    a_1 solved from the R500 point must AGREE, for every object.  That is an over-determined test with no fit.
